From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] gridcraft: plugin seams (toolbar Plugins menu, desktop loader, web bridge forwarding)

Phase 7 WP13 (docs/plugins.md section 6a): the seams through which the domain's extension crate sheets-plugins reaches the app.
- ui-egui: `office_overlay::set_plugin_menu` (per plugin its name and commands, in the interface language) and a "Plugins" menu
  item in the simplified toolbar and its overflow menu, hidden while no plugin is loaded; a command's `ui.status` is the toast.
- desktop app, behind `office-ext`: `sheets_plugins::init()` (the user's enabled plugins, loaded on a thread) and the menu.
- web app, behind `office-ext`, host mode only: `sheets_plugins::init_web()` (the input lock as the command hook) before `ready`;
  `host.rs` forwards `gridcraft:plugin*` messages to sheets-plugins and posts its answers after each frame, and the app keeps
  drawing frames while a call waits for the page. The protocol is in our crates (plugin-adapter), not here.
---

